      title: "CAN YOU PAINT HARDIE BOARD?",
      datePublished: "September 1, 2025",
      meta: "Yes, Hardie board can be painted, but the process requires the right materials and preparation to ensure a durable, long-lasting finish.",
      body: "\n<p>Homeowners often ask whether Hardie board siding can be painted, especially when they’re looking to refresh the exterior of their home. The good news is yes—Hardie board, also known as fiber cement siding, can absolutely be painted. However, achieving a durable, beautiful finish requires the right preparation and paint selection.</p>\n<h3>Why Paint Hardie Board?</h3>\n<p>Hardie board is engineered for durability, but like any exterior material, it is exposed to sunlight, rain, and seasonal temperature shifts. Over time, factory finishes can fade, and color preferences may change. Painting Hardie board allows homeowners to update their curb appeal without replacing siding.</p>\n<h3>Best Paint for Hardie Board</h3>\n<p>Choosing the right paint is crucial. Experts recommend using 100% acrylic exterior paint because it bonds well with fiber cement surfaces and resists peeling or cracking. Avoid oil-based paints, which don’t adhere as effect",
